content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-111 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-21100; reported grinding noise from the non-drive-end bearing.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "The reported 4.2 mm/s vibration falls in Figure 3 Zone B, 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation'. It is 0.3 mm/s below the 4.5 mm/s Zone C boundary ('Restricted - plan maintenance') and below Zone D ('Damage likely - stop the pump'). Figure 3 specifically applies to vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings, and the manual requires readings on both housings with the highest reading classified. Thus the reported value alone does not trigger SSP-07's immediate-stop and reliability-engineer notification rule for the manufacturer's highest severity zone, subject to confirmation of the measurement details.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reported bearing-housing temperature of 74 C exceeds the documented normal limit of up to 70 C by 4 C, but remains 6 C below the 80 C alarm and 16 C below the 90 C trip. Because it is not above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit, SSP-07's requirement to raise a priority-1 work order within the shift is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The non-drive-end bearing grinding noise is itself a documented bearing-replacement trigger: section 5.3 requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature. This defect requires corrective work even though the reported vibration remains in Zone B.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The documented seal requirement is Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and 'never run dry'. If 'seal is dry' means operation without flush, that requirement is being violated and the pump must not be operated dry. If it merely means no visible external leakage, it does not by itself establish dry-running or prove that seal replacement is required; the leakage troubleshooting row links replacement to leakage symptoms and causes such as worn/cracked faces, dry-running or misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P2 is assigned for planned corrective work because the bearing-pair replacement trigger is met, while neither the documented automatic P1 temperature trigger nor the highest-vibration-zone immediate-stop trigger is met by the reported readings. The evidence does not provide P2/P3 completion-time definitions.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Most likely: non-drive-end bearing wear or damage. This is consistent with the grinding noise and elevated housing temperature; bearing wear is listed as a probable cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature. Actual wear remains to be confirmed by inspection, but noise alone already triggers pair replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is the next common documented cause to investigate because it is listed for both high vibration and high bearing temperature; check alignment rather than assuming the bearing is the sole root cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a documented possible cause of the elevated bearing temperature. Check grease quantity; the report provides no grease-quantity finding.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Other documented high-vibration causes requiring checks are impeller imbalance or damage and cavitation. Inspect the impeller and check NPSH while investigating the bearing defect.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before any further running test, establish whether the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge is present and whether 'seal is dry' means dry-running. Never operate the pump with a dry-running seal; if flush is absent, keep the pump out of operation until the flush and seal condition have been addressed.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm that the reported 4.2 mm/s is RMS vibration velocity on a bearing housing, then measure both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. If the highest reading is classified in Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. Also record the individual housing temperatures against the 70 C normal, 80 C alarm and 90 C trip limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before internal or seal work, electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first. Follow the manual requirement to isolate and drain the pump before disassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out and record the troubleshooting checks: grease quantity for the high temperature; alignment for both temperature and vibration; bearing and impeller inspection; and an NPSH/cavitation check. Use these findings to identify the underlying cause rather than treating the bearing replacement as proof of root cause.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Whenever the back pull-out assembly is lifted, use a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment. The assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding SSP-07's 25 kg threshold; the manual also requires lifting equipment for it.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair because the non-drive-end bearing is noisy: install one HF3-510 non-drive-end 6310-C3 bearing and one HF3-512 drive-end 6312-C3 bearing. Do not replace only the noisy bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If seal replacement is authorised after clarifying the dry-seal report, follow section 5.2: remove the back pull-out assembly, remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, and inspect the sleeve for scoring. Fit a new HF3-450 component seal and a new casing gasket. Do not substitute HF3-450B or use the bulletin's pre-set/no-sleeve-measurement instructions on this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket whenever the casing is opened. On reassembly, tighten disturbed fasteners to Table 5 with lightly oiled threads: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm; M24 impeller nut 160 Nm; M10 seal gland nuts 25 Nm; and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm, where applicable to the work performed. The 25 Nm gland-nut value, not the bulletin's 30 Nm, applies to this asset.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before return to service, verify the Plan 11 flush arrangement and do not run the seal dry. Thereafter measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings every week and act on the zone of the highest reading.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace together with the drive-end bearing because either bearing exhibiting noise requires replacement of the pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; required as the other half of the mandatory bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; supply for replacement whenever the casing is opened and when carrying out the documented seal-replacement procedure.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Component-type mechanical seal; conditional on clarification/inspection establishing that seal replacement is required. This is the applicable seal for serial HF3-21100 because it is below HF3-22000; do not use HF3-450B.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For the planned internal work and any seal work, apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit after draining and venting. SSP-07 applies to all site pumps and requires every applicable control to be listed.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use a shift-supervisor-signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly; this exceeds the site's heavier-than-25-kg lifting-control threshold.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the highest bearing-housing vibration reading falls in Figure 3 Zone D, the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The reported 4.2 mm/s value is Zone B, so this is a conditional control rather than a reason for an unconditional immediate stop on the current evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If bearing temperature rises above the manufacturer's 80 C alarm limit, raise a priority-1 work order within the shift; the HF-300 also documents a 90 C trip. The reported 74 C does not activate the P1 rule.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional chemical control: if P-111 is confirmed to be on a chemically dosed line, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The supplied dosing note identifies P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line but does not establish P-111's service, so this must be confirmed before line break.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not conduct running tests with an absent seal flush: the HF-300 uses Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement, only if authorised after the dry-seal clarification and inspection: standard allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment, when required because the work moves the motor or bearing housing: standard allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part and gland-torque conflict: the manual parts list specifies HF3-450 and Table 5 specifies 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies pre-set HF3-450B and 30 Nm. The bulletin applies only to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above and explicitly directs pumps below that serial to continue using HF3-450 and manual Table 5. Serial HF3-21100 is below the boundary, so HF3-450 and 25 Nm apply to P-111; HF3-450B, 30 Nm and the pre-set/no-sleeve-measurement instructions do not.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft-sleeve scoring: manual section 5.2 requires inspection for scoring but supplies no numerical rejection limit. SB-2026-014's instruction to replace HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm is part of the instructions for pumps serial HF3-22000 and above, so it is not an applicable acceptance limit for HF3-21100. Do not apply that threshold to this asset; escalate any scoring for an applicable decision.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is the reported 4.2 mm/s an RMS vibration-velocity measurement on a bearing housing, and what are the separate drive-end and non-drive-end readings? Figure 3 requires mm/s RMS on bearing housings and the manual requires classification of the highest reading from both housings (C06, C07).",
    "Does the 74 C report apply to both housings or only one, and which one? Separate current temperature and vibration trends are not supplied; the applicable housing limits are 70 C normal, 80 C alarm and 90 C trip (C02).",
    "Does 'seal is dry' mean no external leakage, or that the seal/Plan 11 flush has run dry? What is the flush condition, and is seal replacement actually required? The evidence prohibits dry-running but does not establish seal-face condition or provide flush flow/pressure acceptance values (C02, C09, C10).",
    "What are the alignment readings, grease-quantity result, impeller condition and NPSH/cavitation findings? These are required diagnostic checks, and the evidence does not establish which documented possible cause is the root cause (C09).",
    "What grease type and correct grease quantity, and what detailed bearing fits/disassembly requirements, apply? The supplied evidence instructs the technician to check grease quantity and replace the bearings as a pair but does not provide those specifications (C09, C10).",
    "If shaft sleeve HF3-455 is scored, what acceptance/rejection limit applies to serial HF3-21100? The manual excerpt only says to inspect it, and the 0.1 mm bulletin threshold does not apply below HF3-22000 (C10, C13).",
    "Is P-111 on a chemically dosed line or otherwise handling a chemical requiring goggles and nitrile gloves? SSP-07 states the control for chemically dosed lines, while the supplied dosing note identifies only P-101 to P-106 (C15, C16).",
    "What completion window is required for this P2 order? SSP-07 defines the P1-within-shift trigger for temperature above the manufacturer's alarm but gives no P2/P3 priority definitions or due times (C15)."
  ]
}
